## Injecting code

the place where the code is injected is called context

```elixir
defmodule Mod do
  defmacro definfo do
    IO.puts "In macros context (#{__MODULE__})"
    quote do
      IO.puts "In callers contex (#{__MODULE__})"
      def friendly_info do
        IO.puts """
        My name is #{__MODULE__}
        My function are #{inspect __MODULE__.__info__(:functions)}
        """
      end   
    end
  end
end
```

<!-- livebook:{"output":true} -->

```
{:module, Mod, <<70, 79, 82, 49, 0, 0, 12, ...>>, ...}
```

```elixir
defmodule MyModule do
  require Mod
  Mod.definfo 
end

# it will not work inside the same module, cause it looks in the local scope
MyModule.friendly_info
```

<!-- livebook:{"output":true} -->

```
In macros context (Elixir.Mod)
In callers contex (Elixir.MyModule)
My name is Elixir.MyModule
My function are [friendly_info: 0]

```

<!-- livebook:{"output":true} -->

```
:ok
```

macro hygine, means how we access scope beetween, calllers, the cleanes way possible. but sometimes migth be an unnecesary evil

```elixir
ast = quote do
  if meaning_of_life == 42 do
    "its true"
  else
    "tbd"
  end
end
```

<!-- livebook:{"output":true} -->

```
{:if, [context: Elixir, imports: [{2, Kernel}]],
 [
   {:==, [context: Elixir, imports: [{2, Kernel}]], [{:meaning_of_life, [], Elixir}, 42]},
   [do: "its true", else: "tbd"]
 ]}
```

```elixir
Code.eval_quoted(ast)
```

<!-- livebook:{"output":true} -->

```
error: undefined variable "meaning_of_life" (context Elixir)
└─ nofile:1

```

<!-- livebook:{"output":true} -->

```
** (CompileError) cannot compile cell (errors have been logged)
```

the previous error is cause elixir is not able to access the outside scope.

```elixir
ast = quote do
  if var!(meaning_of_life) == 42 do
    "true"
  else
    "false"
  end
end
```

<!-- livebook:{"output":true} -->

```
{:if, [context: Elixir, imports: [{2, Kernel}]],
 [
   {:==, [context: Elixir, imports: [{2, Kernel}]],
    [
      {:var!, [context: Elixir, imports: [{1, Kernel}, {2, Kernel}]],
       [{:meaning_of_life, [], Elixir}]},
      42
    ]},
   [do: "true", else: "false"]
 ]}
```

```elixir
Code.eval_quoted(ast, meaning_of_life: 43)
```

<!-- livebook:{"output":true} -->

```
{"false", [meaning_of_life: 43]}
```

